  "result": "Perfect! All 103 tests pass \u2713\n\nI've successfully added VAT calculation to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js**:\n   - Added `lineVat(line)` function: calculates VAT on the line's amount after discount (`(lineTotal - discount) * vatRate / 100`), rounded per line with `roundCents()`\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n     - vat: sum of all per-line VAT amounts\n     - total = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped to >= 0)\n\n2. **src/render.js**: \n   - Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to display VAT line just above the total\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js**: \n   - Added 6 new tests for `lineVat()` covering various VAT rates and discount scenarios\n   - Updated all `invoiceTotals()` tests to include VAT calculations with per-line rounding\n   - Added test for mixed VAT rates\n\n4. **test/render.test.js**:\n   - Updated all render tests to expect VAT line in output\n   - Fixed line counts and assertions to account for the new VAT line\n   - Added tests for VAT display accuracy\n\n**Key implementation detail**: VAT is calculated and rounded per line, then summed for the invoice total. This means the invoice VAT is never a simple percentage of the invoice total\u2014it's always the sum of the individually-rounded line VATs, as specified.",
